# TAN-SIP order 4 with a deliberately ROUGH order-2 AP/BP (synthetic,
# audit probe d/sip4_inv.hdr). wcslib uses AP/BP only as the starting
# guess and iterates on A/B (dis.h: "used by disx2p() to provide an
# initial estimate for its more precise iterative inversion"); evaluating
# AP/BP as the exact inverse was up to 19.6 px off here.
# TOL_PX 1e-8: the s2p input is wcslib's p2s sky position, whose angular
# round-off (~2e-10 arcsec, the p2s budget measured on every case) is
# 4e-09 px at this case's 0.05 arcsec/px plate scale; measured Go vs wcslib
# max 2.2e-9 px. Known SIP/TPV inverse bugs were >= 1e-4 px.
TOL_PX 1e-8
NOTE pipeline: SIP AP/BP as starting guess only
GRID 1 4096 9 1 4096 9
PIX 2048 2048
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 4096
NAXIS2  = 4096
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TAN-SIP'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TAN-SIP'
CRVAL1  = 150.1166
CRVAL2  = 2.2058
CRPIX1  = 2048.0
CRPIX2  = 2048.0
CD1_1   = -1.3888E-05
CD1_2   = 2.1E-07
CD2_1   = 1.9E-07
CD2_2   = 1.3888E-05
A_ORDER = 4
A_0_2   = 2.1E-06
A_1_1   = -1.4E-05
A_2_0   = 8.2E-06
A_0_3   = 3.1E-10
A_1_2   = -2.2E-10
A_2_1   = 5.1E-10
A_3_0   = -1.3E-10
A_0_4   = 1.1E-14
A_2_2   = -3.0E-14
A_4_0   = 2.0E-14
B_ORDER = 4
B_0_2   = -6.0E-06
B_1_1   = 9.0E-06
B_2_0   = -2.6E-06
B_0_3   = 4.0E-10
B_1_2   = 1.9E-10
B_2_1   = -3.3E-10
B_3_0   = 2.2E-10
B_1_3   = 1.5E-14
B_3_1   = -2.5E-14
B_0_4   = 5.0E-15
AP_ORDER= 2
AP_1_0  = 1.0E-6
AP_0_2  = -2.1E-06
AP_1_1  = 1.4E-05
AP_2_0  = -8.2E-06
BP_ORDER= 2
BP_0_2  = 6.0E-06
BP_1_1  = -9.0E-06
BP_2_0  = 2.6E-06
